From 49d41542f0ccfed448d90c9ad4397a592292d027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MT6762 local experiment <mt6762-build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:51:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm: add explicit BIF generation and ownership laboratory

AI-assisted local experiment, not intended for upstream submission. Model immutable synthetic BIF calibration and TDET state, fresh ADC transitions and scoped failures. An explicit immutable timing override separates protocol tests from unchanged default conversion timing.
---
 docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst        | 24 +++++++++
 hw/arm/mt6762.c                   | 58 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 hw/arm/mt6762_lab_power.c         | 82 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 include/hw/arm/mt6762_lab_power.h | 10 ++++
 tests/mt6762/test_lab_bif.py      | 54 ++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/mt6762/test_lab_power.py    |  5 +-
 6 files changed, 212 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/mt6762/test_lab_bif.py

diff --git a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
index d67b723..8d09ee5 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
@@ -269,3 +269,27 @@ commands, progression, all faults, rejected destructive writes and default
 absence. The XNU loader's ``--native-lab-gauge`` asserts only the matching
 synthetic calibration/ownership contract. These values must never be copied
 into a physical-phone handoff without independent live validation.
+
+Explicit synthetic BIF raw-pair diagnostics
+------------------------------------------
+
+``lab-bif=on`` requires ``lab-power=on``. It supplies invented, already-clear
+TDET/configuration words and a raw BIF output4089, paired with raw NTC1400.
+TDET, ADC trim and configuration writes remain rejected. No battery
+thermistor calibration or temperature is provided. Read-only state reports
+requests, completions and attempted TDET writes; native diagnostic runs must
+leave the latter at zero.
+
+Faults ``bif-tdet-set``, ``bif-config``, ``bif-timeout``, ``bif-stale``,
+``bif-rail`` and ``bif-tdet-changed`` exercise admission, conversion and
+post-conversion ownership checks. ``adc-stale`` affects baseline battery/NTC
+READY generation. ``tests/mt6762/test_lab_bif.py`` checks each independently.
+
+Default NTC/BIF completion remains80 virtual us. The optional immutable
+``lab-adc-delay-us=2000`` slows only those two channels for a separately
+identified protocol test. Valid values are0 (default) or80..10000 and require
+``lab-power``. It does not force READY-low on reads or alter native freshness
+checks. Eight-core and single-core native build17 runs missed the default
+READY-low transition and correctly rejected the raw pair; the explicit
+2000us fixture subsequently exercised successful raw-pair acquisition.
+Neither timing establishes physical PMIC behavior.
